    "result_text": "Done. The full build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`), and the audit log confirms the new format: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` (region `NSW`, FY `27`, HASH8 `16E6609E`, check digit `1`).\n\n## What changed\n\nThe unified `memberId` is `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, assembled in one place and threaded through the existing pipeline with minimal disturbance:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the three DTO fields (`customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`) with a single read-only `memberId`. This is what the test observes (`memberId` present, old two absent).\n2. **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 now builds `region + FY(2-digit) + HASH8 + CHK`, reusing the existing `Locality`, `FiscalYear`, and `CheckDigit` helpers. `CHK` is the Luhn digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`.\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 maps `memberId` from the stored id; dropped the `membershipNumber`/`checkDigit` expressions; and switched `locality`/`timezone` to derive the region directly from postcode/city (they previously parsed the old `-` separator, which the new format doesn't have).\n4. **`SaveOwner.java`** \u2014 audit lines now log `memberId` instead of `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`.\n5. **`MembershipNumber.java`** \u2014 deleted (no longer referenced).\n\n## Design notes on keeping structural impact low\n\n- **The `Owner` entity is untouched.** Its `customer_code` column now simply stores the unified memberId \u2014 a legacy column name behind a renamed concept, which avoids editing a large, high-WMC class and the DB schema. Renaming that field/column would have added the biggest cost multiplier for zero behavioural gain, since the id is invisible at the persistence layer.\n- **`DeduplicateCustomerCode` is untouched.** It already dedupes on the stored id, so collision handling now applies to the memberId for free \u2014 the spec's requirement is met without a change.\n- **Fiscal year and owner segment** stay consistent with the memberId: the FY inside the id and the `fiscalYear` field both come from `FiscalYear.of(registrationDate)`, and the owner segment keys off `locality`, which is the same region prefix embedded in the id.\n\nOne deliberate trade-off worth flagging: the persistence field and the two function classes (`AssignCustomerCode`, `DeduplicateCustomerCode`) keep their old `CustomerCode` names internally even though they now operate on the memberId. Renaming them for clarity would touch `Owner.java`, the HSQLDB schema, and `owners.POST.yml`. I left them as-is to minimize structural impact per the brief \u2014 say the word if you'd prefer the fuller rename.",
